#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""asc-ctl - limited, audited Docker operations for the AI Stream Clipper project.

Installed root-owned at /usr/local/sbin/asc-ctl and allowed to the `asc` user via
/etc/sudoers.d/asc-ctl. It replaces membership of the `docker` group (which is
root-equivalent) with a fixed set of operations that can only touch the compose project
"asc" and only run configurations that pass the isolation policy below.

Policy (checked on the *resolved* compose config, which is then the exact file executed):
  * project name "asc"; container names "asc-*"; images ai-stream-clipper[-vision]:<tag>
    or postgres:16.x; no build sections (images are built with `asc-ctl build`)
  * no privileged, cap_add, host network/pid/ipc/uts/userns/cgroup, sysctls, runtime,
    volumes_from, secrets/configs, unconfined security options, user root
  * bind mounts only below /opt/asc/ or /etc/asc/tls (the latter read-only)
  * named volumes / networks only asc_* and never external
  * devices only /dev/dri/renderD128 (GPU hosts), group_add only the render gid
  * published ports only 8780/8781 on this server's LAN IP (or 127.0.0.1)
  * 212 (dedicated database host, shared with other projects): ONLY the asc PostgreSQL, published
    only on 192.168.1.212:55432, client access limited by its own pg_hba (the 210 API host)
  * every service declares CPU and memory limits
  * bench-pr31 on 201 runs one separately labelled sandbox with pinned inputs and no network
Never runs `docker system prune`, `down -v`, or anything on other projects.
"""

